  "title": "Start from the first person, not the world",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "86e6ac9c-3a50-4c2b-8428-21af8146af43",
      "text": "The foundational question of physics should be what an observer will experience next, not what is the case in the world. A theory built on the first-person perspective is to be explored as an alternative to one built on the third-person world.",
